from: ta-gate-observability
session: ta-gate-observability implementation (PR E)

## What changed

Worktree/branch `ta-gate-observability` (already existed off `main@f5261c8e`, includes merged
A' #1479 + D #1481). Implemented the full plan (`planning/ta-gate-observability-plan.md`) in 2
commits:

- `033b0529` refactor(config): extract ThroughputAnalyzerEnabled onto config.Config — pure
  refactor, moves the enablement predicate from package `main` to `(*Config).ThroughputAnalyzerEnabled()`;
  migrated `TestThroughputAnalyzerEnabled` to `internal/config` as `TestConfig_ThroughputAnalyzerEnabled`;
  deleted `cmd/main_test.go` (its only test moved).
- `67ac0476` feat(controller): warn when a live ConfigMap edit can't change TA registration —
  adds `ConfigMapReconciler.ThroughputRegistered` field, captured once in `cmd/main.go` from the
  same value used for the startup registration gate; `handleSaturationConfigMap`'s global path now
  emits a K8s Warning event (reason `ThroughputAnalyzerRestartRequired`, new constant in
  `internal/constants/constants.go`) + a restart-instruction log line when live TA-enablement
  diverges from the frozen startup decision, in both directions. Namespace-local ConfigMaps are
  explicitly out of scope (non-goal, confirmed by test).

All gates green: `make test` (full suite incl. `internal/controller` envtest suite, 35/35 specs),
`make lint` (0 issues), `gofmt` clean, `go build ./...` clean, DCO signed on both commits, §4a
plans-branch-identifier grep clean. Dev-guide (`docs/developer-guide/throughput-analyzer.md`)
updated with the new Warning-event/restart-log behavior and the namespace-local limitation,
framed as current behavior (no forward-looking "pending PR" language).

Full detail in `session/status/ta-gate-observability.md`, including two coder-judgment notes
worth preserving: (1) splitting the plan's 2-commit structure required staging + stashing +
rebuilding each commit's isolated tree, since both commits touch the same `cmd/main.go` call
site; (2) fixed a test-isolation collision the new reconciler tests introduced (added
`DeferCleanup` rather than changing the pre-existing test).

Written a `review__ta-gate-observability-ready.md` trigger per CODER-CONVENTIONS §5.4 — internal
review has not yet run. Per §5.4, **not** requesting push authorization in this handoff; that
follows once the review closes clean.

